WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.160
- But I had no idea,
everyone make fun of me now,

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.756
I had no idea who your parents were.

00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:09.250
- (laughs)
- Right, not everybody does.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.923
- Until last night,

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.850
until last night,

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.990
I was like why they keep
talking about the Mamas

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.343
and the Papas and the Beach Boys?

00:00:17.343 --> 00:00:19.042
I was like I love the Mamas and the Papas

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:19.875
and the Beach Boys, I was like,

00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:20.708
what does this have to do with,

00:00:20.708 --> 00:00:21.708
and I was like, what?

00:00:21.708 --> 00:00:24.773
I was like, I had no idea,
I just want you to know,

00:00:25.916 --> 00:00:27.860
on your own merit, I was there,

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.571
and it had nothing to do
with parents or anything,

00:00:30.571 --> 00:00:33.440
and I think that that's kinda something.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.650
To grow up, and I imagine
that was very hard,

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.560
I'm gauging and navigating
that with my kids,

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.170
I'm sure you have to as well,

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:41.940
but being in the public eye,
having parents so famous,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.360
and trying to navigate
that, and what is normal,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.840
and how do I?

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.530
- There was no normal.
- It's so hard.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.290
- That was our normal, chaos.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.443
- I know, that's not good.
- Well,

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.270
- Says my therapist.
- Yeah, right,

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.700
but we also have a great mom, Marylin,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.760
who's in the audience
today, our mother Marylin.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.350
But she was really

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.930
great at keeping it steady

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.910
and being real about things.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.860
Not everything is normal, what is normal?

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.900
Building our self esteem as
people, and showing us love.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.700
And now we instill that in our kids.

00:01:20.576 --> 00:01:21.409
It's important.
- Yeah,

00:01:21.409 --> 00:01:23.344
it's a weird thing to
navigate, but I know,

00:01:23.344 --> 00:01:27.987
since finding that out, I kind
of read in the thing that,

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.990
one of you was put to
bed by Sir Elton John?

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:33.567
- Uh huh, yeah.
- And I was like, what?

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:36.770
(laughs) What is your life? That's insane.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.550
What was he doing at your house.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:39.860
- He just did a lullaby or something?

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:40.970
I don't get it, what?
- No, no, no,

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:45.120
he reminded me, when I was
just on The Talk with him,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.907
a couple years ago that,

00:01:46.907 --> 00:01:48.850
"Don't you remember I put you to sleep?"

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.373
And I'm like, what?

00:01:50.373 --> 00:01:52.070
- I was like, no, but I'm
telling everyone (laughs)

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.550
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:56.883
He literally came, well he
wanted to buy Dad's piano,

00:01:58.001 --> 00:02:00.619
that Dad wrote Good Vibrations
on, that was his mission.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:01.680
- Solid piano.
- Solid piano,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.990
lot of memories there,
and he wanted this piano.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.910
He came over, and he was
probably begging for it,

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.060
my mom said "No,"

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.750
but I guess I came downstairs
when they were chatting

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.790
and doing their thing, and he
said "Time to go back to bed,"

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.690
and put me in my bed, and that was it,

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:14.550
Elton John put me to sleep.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:18.010
- Okay, the best part, it
turns out, of this story,

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.100
actually isn't that,

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.357
it's the fact that your mom was like

00:02:20.357 --> 00:02:21.550
"No, you can't have our piano."

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:25.261
- I know.
- To Elton John (laughs)

00:02:25.261 --> 00:02:26.750
- Well guess what, that piano's mine now

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.900
so I'm very very happy.

